        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Text output bypasses cobra's output writer",
        "explanation": "fmt.Println writes straight to the process stdout and ignores the writer configured on the command (cmd.SetOut), so tests or callers that redirect output won't capture it. Every other command in this file writes through cmd. It also prints a raw Go slice such as \"[grpc k8s]\" instead of readable lines.",
        "suggestion": "Write each domain to cmd.OutOrStdout(), e.g. `for _, d := range res.Domains { fmt.Fprintln(cmd.OutOrStdout(), d) }`.",
